<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
                      http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.29.xsd"
    objectQuotingStrategy="QUOTE_ONLY_RESERVED_WORDS">

    <!--
      Records, at every start, what a rolled-back release left unrecorded. Server 6.5.4 writes no revisions: if
      production runs it again after step C, its uploads raise lock_version without a revision and its new
      submissions have none. On the next start of a release with the journal, this writes one explicit gap revision
      for each such submission: kind BASELINE, command GAP_REPAIR, actor MIGRATION, at the current lock_version,
      with previous_version naming the head it jumps from (NULL for a submission created in the window). The
      versions in between are recorded as unknown, never as silent.

      It skips a submission that has a revision at or above its lock_version. One whose head is above it cannot
      happen through the application; the reconciliation check reports it, and so a start never fails on it. A
      write that changed a row without raising its version (hand-written SQL) is not a gap this can record; the
      reconciliation check reports that too.

      Cost: one index probe per submission; with no gap it writes nothing (see the rehearsal numbers in
      docs/agent-context/active-production-interface.md). runAlways: Liquibase runs it on every update, in its place
      after the journal's other changesets.

      Rollback: nothing to undo; the gap revisions stay with the journal. It refuses nothing either: this changeset
      runs at every start, and Liquibase records each run as the latest, so every later rollback begins here. A
      refusal here would block those, unrelated ones included; the rollbacks that remove a guard refuse instead.
    -->
    <changeSet id="20261124-c08-submission-revision-gap-repair" author="datarun" runAlways="true">
        <sql>
            INSERT INTO journal.submission_revision (submission_id, version, previous_version, kind, command, actor_system,
                                             form_data, metadata)
            SELECT s.id, s.lock_version,
                   (SELECT max(h.version) FROM journal.submission_revision h WHERE h.submission_id = s.id),
                   'BASELINE', 'GAP_REPAIR', 'MIGRATION', s.form_data, journal.submission_revision_metadata(s)
            FROM data_submission s
            WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM journal.submission_revision r
                              WHERE r.submission_id = s.id AND r.version >= s.lock_version)
        </sql>
        <rollback/>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
